{"title":"Career roadmap · Avionics Engineer","role":"Avionics Engineer","summary":"An Avionics Engineer designs, integrates, tests and maintains the electronic and computer systems used in aircraft and spacecraft. These systems include navigation, communication, flight control, instrumentation, radar, embedded computers, displays, sensors and electrical/electronic interfaces.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Avionics/embedded intern, avionics engineer trainee, test engineer, aerospace electronics engineer"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"What should I specialise in?","output":"Flight-control electronics, navigation, communication, embedded avionics, aircraft systems or verification"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Avionics Engineer, Systems Engineer, Avionics Integration Lead or specialist engineer"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How do I remain relevant?","output":"Avionics Architect, Chief Systems Engineer, Flight Systems Lead or aerospace engineering manager"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For an Aerospace/Aeronautical Engineering graduate, this is a directly aligned career. The strongest profile combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Avionics","Embedded Systems","Electronics","Control Systems","Communication","Aerospace Software"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build this","Key skills","Proof of progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Electronics + programming foundation"},{"text":"C/C++, Python, circuits, digital electronics, mathematics"},{"text":"Microcontroller-based aerospace sensor project"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Avionics fundamentals"},{"text":"Sensors, embedded systems, communication, navigation, control"},{"text":"Aircraft instrumentation prototype"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Flight sy